_1} → [TopologicalSpace.{u_1} X] → Set.{u_1} X → Prop","unsafe":false,"value":64,"source":{"code":"/-- A preirreducible set `s` is one where there is no non-trivial pair of disjoint opens on `s`. -/\ndef IsPreirreducible (s : Set X) : Prop :=\n  ∀ u v : Set X, IsOpen u → IsOpen v → (s ∩ u).Nonempty → (s ∩ v).Nonempty → (s ∩ (u ∩ v)).Nonempty","start":43,"end":45},"axioms":[]}